    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d277">

                <pb facs="0376" n="302" sameAs="frus:frus1866p1/pg302"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Bigelow</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 445.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-05-01"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 1, 1866.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I enclose herewith, for your information,
                    copy of a letter, of the 11th ultimo, which I addressed to the Hon. William
                    Dennison, the Postmaster General, in reply to his inquiry for my opinion in
                    regard to the offer of the French government of their line of steam ocean
                    packets to convey the United States mail between New Orleans and Vera Cruz.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Bigelow</hi>, Esq.,<hi rendition="#italic">
                            &amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d277-a1.xml" xpointer="d277-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
